    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only real test class (the other two are base/helper classes). Both tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\nThe change is complete and the test suite is green. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required exposing a computed `ownerSegment` property (`<TIER>_<AREA>`) on owners.\n\n**1. `src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getOwnerSegment()` method next to the existing computed `getLocality()`/`getTimezone()`:\n- **TIER** = `PREMIUM` when `getMembershipLevel() >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n- **AREA** = `METRO` when the locality is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD \u2014 reusing the existing `REGION_TIMEZONE` region map), else `REGIONAL`.\n\n**2. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the Owner schema (after `timezone`). The DTO is generated from this spec, and MapStruct auto-maps the matching `getOwnerSegment()` getter into the response \u2014 the same mechanism already used for `locality` and `timezone`, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass:\n- `coreSegmentForKnownRegion` \u2192 Sydney (NSW), level 2 \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO` \u2705\n- `functionalitySegmentForUnknownRegion` \u2192 unknown city, level 2 \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL` \u2705\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0.",
